    {
      "line_start": 4,
      "line_end": 6,
      "text": "The memory model processes each meeting to generate a summary and a list of action items. When a topic from a previous meeting is discussed again, the system updates the corresponding memory entry.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 7,
      "line_end": 11,
      "text": "The demonstration illustrates the memory update process: Meeting 16's transcript creates an initial memory from scratch. Meeting 17's transcript is then processed along with the existing memory from 16 to produce an updated version, adding new items and modifying existing ones.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 12,
      "line_end": 18,
      "text": "When a topic is revisited in a subsequent meeting, its memory item is updated to reflect new developments. For example, an item that was a \"TODO\" in meeting 16 could be updated in meeting 17 with progress reports or new observations.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 12,
      "line_end": 21,
      "text": "The current update mechanism for a revisited item involves updating its associated `meeting ID` to the current meeting's ID (e.g., from 16 to 17) and appending new information.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 19,
      "line_end": 20,
      "text": "A suggestion was made to implement dynamic time tracking, where an item's temporal reference (e.g., \"this meeting\") would automatically update to \"one week ago\" in the following week's meeting. This would require updating all time-related references whenever a new meeting's memory is integrated.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 21,
      "line_end": 21,
      "text": "The current system tracks items by `meeting ID` rather than relative time (e.g., \"one week ago\"), which makes the suggested dynamic temporal updates not directly implementable with the current design.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 21,
      "line_end": 22,
      "text": "The system includes a forgetting mechanism: an item that is not discussed within a predefined window (e.g., three meetings) will be deleted from the memory.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    }
